IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `hcc-dates`
IMPORT `hcc-complaints`

-- Health Care Complaints Act 1993 (NSW) -- worked cases for every exported question in hcc-complaints.l4.
-- Every expected value was worked by hand from the deposited text; none was copied from the encoding's output. Each
-- assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Dates are illustrative.
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `cases`

`d` MEANS `the date`

`conduct` MEANS `the professional conduct of a health practitioner`
`care` MEANS `a health service that affects or is likely to affect the clinical management or care of an individual client`
`PHA breach` MEANS `a breach of Part 7 Division 1 or 3 of the Public Health Act 2010, or its code of conduct, by a health organisation`
`no care` MEANS `a health service that does not affect the clinical management or care of any individual client`
`other matter` MEANS `something else`

`public` MEANS `a public health organisation or public hospital under the Health Services Act 1997`
`private facility` MEANS `a private health facility licensed under the Private Health Facilities Act 2007`
`excluded` MEANS `an organisation the regulations exclude`
`other org` MEANS `any other health organisation`

`practitioner` MEANS `a health practitioner`
`organisation` MEANS `a health organisation`

`investigate` MEANS `to investigate the complaint`
`conciliate` MEANS `to refer the complaint for conciliation`
`div 9` MEANS `to deal with the complaint under Division 9 (complaints resolution)`
`to Secretary` MEANS `to refer the complaint to the Health Secretary (s 25 or 25A)`
`to council` MEANS `to refer the complaint to a professional council or another person or body (s 25B or 26)`
`discontinue` MEANS `to discontinue dealing with the complaint (s 27)`

`in time` MEANS `done in time`
`late` MEANS `done late`
`passed` MEANS `not done, and the time has passed`
`not yet` MEANS `not done yet, and the time has not passed`
`not required` MEANS `no time limit applies, because it was not required`

`party` MEANS `a party to the complaint (the complainant or the person complained about)`
`client` MEANS `the client whose treatment it is, not a party`
`contact` MEANS `the client's contact recorded by the hospital or health care facility`
`associate` MEANS `another person associated with the client, such as a legal representative of the client or the client's estate`

`s98` MEANS `persuading by threat, intimidation or inducement, or victimising, a complainant (s 98)`
`s99` MEANS `knowingly giving the Commission false or misleading information (s 99)`
`s97A` MEANS `knowingly giving the Commissioner or the Commission's staff false or misleading information about a complaint (s 97A(d))`
`s58` MEANS `a conciliator or Registry staff member disclosing information from conciliation (s 58)`
`s99A` MEANS `improperly disclosing information obtained under the Act (s 99A)`

§§ `s 4 -- relevant health organisation`

-- A "means ... other than" definition: each excluded kind is no.
#ASSERT `Is it a relevant health organisation` `other org` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is it a relevant health organisation` `public` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is it a relevant health organisation` `private facility` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is it a relevant health organisation` `excluded` EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `ss 7, 8 -- what a complaint can be about`

#ASSERT `Can I make a complaint about this` `conduct` `other org` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I make a complaint about this` `care` `public` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A cosmetic clinic (any other organisation) breaching the Public Health Act code: (a1).
#ASSERT `Can I make a complaint about this` `PHA breach` `other org` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The same breach by a public hospital is outside (a1): the Act does not answer under (a1) (fork F2).
#ASSERT `Can I make a complaint about this` `PHA breach` `public` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Can I make a complaint about this` `PHA breach` `private facility` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Can I make a complaint about this` `no care` `other org` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Can I make a complaint about this` `other matter` `other org` EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 4 -- complainant`

#ASSERT `Am I the complainant` `I made it myself` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I the complainant` `a representative I chose made it on my behalf, about my care` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The lawyer the client chose to make the complaint is not the complainant: the client is (s 4(b)).
#ASSERT `Am I the complainant` `I made it as the representative the client chose` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The client, when a relative made it without being chosen as representative: the relative is the complainant (s 4(a)).
#ASSERT `Am I the complainant` `someone else made it about my care, not as a representative I chose` EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `s 9 -- making the complaint`

#ASSERT `Has my complaint been made` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Has my complaint been made` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Only a telephone call: not yet made.
#ASSERT `Has my complaint been made` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Must the Commission's staff help me make my complaint` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Must the Commission's staff help me make my complaint` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `ss 16, 16A, 17 -- who is told of the complaint`

#ASSERT `Must the person I complain about be told of my complaint and who I am` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Risk of intimidation to me: not required ...
#ASSERT `Must the person I complain about be told of my complaint and who I am` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- ... unless natural justice makes it essential.
#ASSERT `Must the person I complain about be told of my complaint and who I am` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Must the person I complain about be told of my complaint and who I am` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- Assessed 20 January 2026: 14 days later is 3 February 2026.
#ASSERT `By what day must the person I complain about be told` (`d` 20 1 2026) EQUALS `d` 3 2 2026
-- Across the year end: 25 December 2025 plus 14 days is 8 January 2026.
#ASSERT `By what day must the person I complain about be told` (`d` 25 12 2025) EQUALS `d` 8 1 2026
-- 20 January 2026 plus 60 days: 11 to 31 January, 28 to 28 February, 21 to 21 March.
#ASSERT `When must the Commission first review its decision not to tell the person` (`d` 20 1 2026) EQUALS `d` 21 3 2026

#ASSERT `Must the practitioner's employer be told of my complaint and who I am` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Must the practitioner's employer be told of my complaint and who I am` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Must the practitioner's employer be told of my complaint and who I am` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Must the practitioner's employer be told of my complaint and who I am` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

#ASSERT `Must the Health Secretary be told of my complaint and who I am` `organisation` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Must the Health Secretary be told of my complaint and who I am` `practitioner` EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `s 18 -- withdrawing`

#ASSERT `Can I withdraw my complaint` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I withdraw my complaint` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I withdraw my complaint` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The client's chosen representative is not the complainant: s 18 does not speak to them.
#ASSERT `Can I withdraw my complaint` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

#ASSERT `If I withdraw, must the Commission still deal with the matter` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `If I withdraw, must the Commission still deal with the matter` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `If I withdraw, must the Commission still deal with the matter` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `If I withdraw, must the Commission still deal with the matter` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `If I withdraw, must the Commission still deal with the matter` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `If I withdraw, must the Commission still deal with the matter` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE

§§ `ss 20-22 -- assessment and its deadline`

#ASSERT `Must the Commission check the allegations with me` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Must the Commission check the allegations with me` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- Required 1 March 2026; 30 April 2026 is 60 days on (30 in March, 30 in April): allowed. 1 May is 61: not allowed.
#ASSERT `Is the time for further particulars within the limit` (`d` 1 3 2026) (`d` 30 4 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is the time for further particulars within the limit` (`d` 1 3 2026) (`d` 1 5 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- Received 1 March 2026: 60 days after is 30 April 2026.
#ASSERT `By what day must the Commission finish assessing my complaint` (`d` 1 3 2026) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2026) EQUALS `d` 30 4 2026
-- Particulars specified for 15 May 2026: 16 to 31 May, 30 to 30 June, 14 to 14 July 2026.
#ASSERT `By what day must the Commission finish assessing my complaint` (`d` 1 3 2026) TRUE (`d` 15 5 2026) EQUALS `d` 14 7 2026
-- A leap year: received 1 February 2028; 28 to 29 February, 31 to 31 March, 1 to 1 April 2028.
#ASSERT `By what day must the Commission finish assessing my complaint` (`d` 1 2 2028) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2028) EQUALS `d` 1 4 2028

-- The s 22 rule. Received 1 March 2026; the last day is 30 April 2026.
#ASSERT `Has the Commission assessed my complaint in time` (`d` 1 3 2026) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2026) TRUE (`d` 30 4 2026) (`d` 1 6 2026) EQUALS `in time`
#ASSERT `Has the Commission assessed my complaint in time` (`d` 1 3 2026) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2026) TRUE (`d` 2 3 2026) (`d` 1 6 2026) EQUALS `in time`
#ASSERT `Has the Commission assessed my complaint in time` (`d` 1 3 2026) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2026) TRUE (`d` 1 5 2026) (`d` 1 6 2026) EQUALS `late`
#ASSERT `Has the Commission assessed my complaint in time` (`d` 1 3 2026) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2026) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2026) (`d` 30 4 2026) EQUALS `not yet`
#ASSERT `Has the Commission assessed my complaint in time` (`d` 1 3 2026) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2026) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2026) (`d` 1 5 2026) EQUALS `passed`
-- With particulars specified for 15 May 2026, the last day is 14 July 2026.
#ASSERT `Has the Commission assessed my complaint in time` (`d` 1 3 2026) TRUE (`d` 15 5 2026) TRUE (`d` 14 7 2026) (`d` 1 8 2026) EQUALS `in time`
#ASSERT `Has the Commission assessed my complaint in time` (`d` 1 3 2026) TRUE (`d` 15 5 2026) TRUE (`d` 15 7 2026) (`d` 1 8 2026) EQUALS `late`
#ASSERT `Has the Commission assessed my complaint in time` (`d` 1 3 2026) TRUE (`d` 15 5 2026) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2026) (`d` 15 7 2026) EQUALS `passed`
-- On 1 May 2026 an assessment not yet done is not late when particulars were asked for.
#ASSERT `Has the Commission assessed my complaint in time` (`d` 1 3 2026) TRUE (`d` 15 5 2026) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2026) (`d` 1 5 2026) EQUALS `not yet`

-- Finding 9 at its widest: received 1 March 2026; particulars required on the 60th day, 30 April 2026, and specified
-- for 60 days later, 29 June 2026 (31 to 31 May, 60 to 29 June); the assessment is then due 60 days after that,
-- 28 August 2026 (1 to 30 June, 32 to 31 July, 60 to 28 August): 180 days after receipt (30 + 30 + 31 + 30 + 31 + 28).
#ASSERT `Is the time for further particulars within the limit` (`d` 30 4 2026) (`d` 29 6 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `By what day must the Commission finish assessing my complaint` (`d` 1 3 2026) TRUE (`d` 29 6 2026) EQUALS `d` 28 8 2026
#ASSERT `Has the Commission assessed my complaint in time` (`d` 1 3 2026) TRUE (`d` 29 6 2026) TRUE (`d` 28 8 2026) (`d` 1 9 2026) EQUALS `in time`
#ASSERT `Has the Commission assessed my complaint in time` (`d` 1 3 2026) TRUE (`d` 29 6 2026) TRUE (`d` 29 8 2026) (`d` 1 9 2026) EQUALS `late`

-- The periods are written once and used by both the MUST rules and the date questions.
#ASSERT `the days for the assessment (s 22)` EQUALS 60
#ASSERT `the days for notice of the assessment decision (s 28(1))` EQUALS 14

§§ `ss 13(1), 23 -- must it investigate`

#ASSERT `Must the Commission investigate my complaint` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Must the Commission investigate my complaint` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Must the Commission investigate my complaint` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Must the Commission investigate my complaint` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Must the Commission investigate my complaint` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Must the Commission investigate my complaint` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Must the Commission investigate my complaint` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE

§§ `s 27 -- discontinuing`

-- Five years to the day is not "more than 5 years"; one day more is.
#ASSERT `Did the matter happen more than 5 years before my complaint` (`d` 1 3 2015) (`d` 1 3 2020) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Did the matter happen more than 5 years before my complaint` (`d` 1 3 2015) (`d` 2 3 2020) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Did the matter happen more than 5 years before my complaint` (`d` 1 3 2023) (`d` 1 3 2026) EQUALS FALSE
-- Complaint on 29 February 2024: five years back is 28 February 2019 (fork F1).
#ASSERT `Did the matter happen more than 5 years before my complaint` (`d` 28 2 2019) (`d` 29 2 2024) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Did the matter happen more than 5 years before my complaint` (`d` 27 2 2019) (`d` 29 2 2024) EQUALS TRUE

-- Arguments: referred under 25A/25B; public health; frivolous; trivial; elsewhere or in court; referred elsewhere;
-- alternative; day it happened; day made; sufficient reason for delay; particulars; Commonwealth.
#ASSERT `Can the Commission discontinue my complaint` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (`d` 1 3 2024) (`d` 1 3 2026) FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `section 27(1) gives no reason on these facts, but its list is not exhaustive (s 27(2))`
#ASSERT `Can the Commission discontinue my complaint` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (`d` 1 3 2024) (`d` 1 3 2026) FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the Commission may discontinue, for a reason section 27(1) gives`
#ASSERT `Can the Commission discontinue my complaint` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE (`d` 1 3 2024) (`d` 1 3 2026) FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the Commission may discontinue, for a reason section 27(1) gives`
-- My negligence claim in court about the same matter: s 27(1)(c).
#ASSERT `Can the Commission discontinue my complaint` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE (`d` 1 3 2024) (`d` 1 3 2026) FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the Commission may discontinue, for a reason section 27(1) gives`
#ASSERT `Can the Commission discontinue my complaint` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE (`d` 1 3 2024) (`d` 1 3 2026) FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the Commission may discontinue, for a reason section 27(1) gives`
#ASSERT `Can the Commission discontinue my complaint` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE (`d` 1 3 2024) (`d` 1 3 2026) FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the Commission may discontinue, for a reason section 27(1) gives`
-- An old matter: more than 5 years, no sufficient reason -> (f); with a sufficient reason -> no reason on these facts.
#ASSERT `Can the Commission discontinue my complaint` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (`d` 1 3 2020) (`d` 2 3 2025) FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the Commission may discontinue, for a reason section 27(1) gives`
#ASSERT `Can the Commission discontinue my complaint` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (`d` 1 3 2020) (`d` 2 3 2025) TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `section 27(1) gives no reason on these facts, but its list is not exhaustive (s 27(2))`
-- Exactly 5 years: (f) does not reach it.
#ASSERT `Can the Commission discontinue my complaint` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (`d` 1 3 2020) (`d` 1 3 2025) FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `section 27(1) gives no reason on these facts, but its list is not exhaustive (s 27(2))`
#ASSERT `Can the Commission discontinue my complaint` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (`d` 1 3 2024) (`d` 1 3 2026) FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `the Commission may discontinue, for a reason section 27(1) gives`
#ASSERT `Can the Commission discontinue my complaint` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (`d` 1 3 2024) (`d` 1 3 2026) FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `the Commission may discontinue, for a reason section 27(1) gives`
-- A public health issue stops discontinuance under s 27, even with a reason ...
#ASSERT `Can the Commission discontinue my complaint` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (`d` 1 3 2024) (`d` 1 3 2026) FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the Commission must not discontinue under section 27, because a significant issue of public health or safety appears`
-- ... but not after a referral under s 25A or 25B ("Despite section 27(3)").
#ASSERT `Can the Commission discontinue my complaint` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (`d` 1 3 2024) (`d` 1 3 2026) FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the Commission must discontinue, because it referred the complaint to the Health Secretary or a professional council (s 25A(2) or 25B(2))`

§§ `s 28 -- notice of the assessment decision, and review`

-- Decision on 10 June 2026: notice by 24 June 2026.
#ASSERT `By what day must I be told the assessment decision` (`d` 10 6 2026) EQUALS `d` 24 6 2026
-- Arguments: decision; s 28(4) risk; override; day of decision; told; day told; today.
#ASSERT `Was I told of the assessment decision in time` `discontinue` FALSE FALSE (`d` 10 6 2026) TRUE (`d` 24 6 2026) (`d` 1 7 2026) EQUALS `in time`
#ASSERT `Was I told of the assessment decision in time` `discontinue` FALSE FALSE (`d` 10 6 2026) TRUE (`d` 25 6 2026) (`d` 1 7 2026) EQUALS `late`
#ASSERT `Was I told of the assessment decision in time` `discontinue` FALSE FALSE (`d` 10 6 2026) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2026) (`d` 24 6 2026) EQUALS `not yet`
#ASSERT `Was I told of the assessment decision in time` `discontinue` FALSE FALSE (`d` 10 6 2026) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2026) (`d` 25 6 2026) EQUALS `passed`
-- A decision to investigate with a s 28(4) risk and no override: notice not required.
#ASSERT `Was I told of the assessment decision in time` `investigate` TRUE FALSE (`d` 10 6 2026) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2026) (`d` 1 7 2026) EQUALS `not required`
#ASSERT `Was I told of the assessment decision in time` `investigate` TRUE TRUE (`d` 10 6 2026) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2026) (`d` 1 7 2026) EQUALS `passed`
#ASSERT `Was I told of the assessment decision in time` `investigate` FALSE FALSE (`d` 10 6 2026) TRUE (`d` 11 6 2026) (`d` 1 7 2026) EQUALS `in time`
-- s 28(4) excuses only notice of a decision to investigate: for conciliation the risk does not matter.
#ASSERT `Was I told of the assessment decision in time` `conciliate` TRUE FALSE (`d` 10 6 2026) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2026) (`d` 1 7 2026) EQUALS `passed`

#ASSERT `Must the notice tell me I can ask for a review` `investigate` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Must the notice tell me I can ask for a review` `conciliate` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Must the notice tell me I can ask for a review` `div 9` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Must the notice tell me I can ask for a review` `to Secretary` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Must the notice tell me I can ask for a review` `to council` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Must the notice tell me I can ask for a review` `discontinue` EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- Notified 3 August 2026: 28 days later is 31 August 2026.
#ASSERT `By what day must I ask for a review of the assessment decision` (`d` 3 8 2026) EQUALS `d` 31 8 2026
-- Notified 15 February 2027: 13 to 28 February, 15 to 15 March 2027.
#ASSERT `By what day must I ask for a review of the assessment decision` (`d` 15 2 2027) EQUALS `d` 15 3 2027
#ASSERT `Must the Commission review its assessment decision` TRUE (`d` 3 8 2026) (`d` 31 8 2026) EQUALS `the Commission must review it`
#ASSERT `Must the Commission review its assessment decision` TRUE (`d` 3 8 2026) (`d` 3 8 2026) EQUALS `the Commission must review it`
#ASSERT `Must the Commission review its assessment decision` TRUE (`d` 3 8 2026) (`d` 1 9 2026) EQUALS `the Commission may review it, but need not, because the 28 days have passed`
#ASSERT `Must the Commission review its assessment decision` FALSE (`d` 3 8 2026) (`d` 10 8 2026) EQUALS `section 28(9) gives no review, because only the complainant may ask`

-- ss 28(7), 28A(9). Decided to investigate 10 June 2026: 20 to 30 June, 51 to 31 July, 60 to 9 August 2026.
#ASSERT `When must the Commission first review its decision not to give notice of the investigation` (`d` 10 6 2026) EQUALS `d` 9 8 2026
-- Decided 15 December 2026: 16 to 31 December, 47 to 31 January, 60 to 13 February 2027.
#ASSERT `When must the Commission first review its decision not to give notice of the investigation` (`d` 15 12 2026) EQUALS `d` 13 2 2027

§§ `s 28A -- the client and the client's family`

-- Arguments: who I am; client died; client incapable; representative consented; s 28A(6) risk; override.
#ASSERT `Is the Commission to tell me the outcome of the assessment` `party` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `section 28 applies to you instead, as a party`
#ASSERT `Is the Commission to tell me the outcome of the assessment` `client` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the Commission must use its best endeavours to tell you`
#ASSERT `Is the Commission to tell me the outcome of the assessment` `client` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `section 28A puts no duty on the Commission to tell you`
#ASSERT `Is the Commission to tell me the outcome of the assessment` `client` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `the Commission need not tell you, because of a risk in section 28A(6)`
#ASSERT `Is the Commission to tell me the outcome of the assessment` `client` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `the Commission must use its best endeavours to tell you`
-- The hospital's recorded contact for a patient who died.
#ASSERT `Is the Commission to tell me the outcome of the assessment` `contact` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the Commission must use its best endeavours to tell you`
-- The contact for a living, capable patient: s 28A(4) forbids it.
#ASSERT `Is the Commission to tell me the outcome of the assessment` `contact` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the Commission may not tell you under section 28A`
-- Incapable patient: only with the authorised representative's consent.
#ASSERT `Is the Commission to tell me the outcome of the assessment` `contact` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the Commission may not tell you under section 28A`
#ASSERT `Is the Commission to tell me the outcome of the assessment` `contact` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the Commission must use its best endeavours to tell you`
#ASSERT `Is the Commission to tell me the outcome of the assessment` `contact` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `the Commission need not tell you, because of a risk in section 28A(6)`
-- The estate's lawyer, the patient having died.
#ASSERT `Is the Commission to tell me the outcome of the assessment` `associate` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the Commission may tell you, if it thinks it appropriate and practicable`
#ASSERT `Is the Commission to tell me the outcome of the assessment` `associate` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the Commission may not tell you under section 28A`
#ASSERT `Is the Commission to tell me the outcome of the assessment` `associate` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `the Commission need not tell you, because of a risk in section 28A(6)`

§§ `ss 39-45, 90CA -- after the investigation`

#ASSERT `What can the Commission do at the end of the investigation` `practitioner` EQUALS LIST `refer the complaint to the Director of Proceedings, who decides whether it is prosecuted before a disciplinary body`, `refer the complaint to the professional council (for example for performance or impairment assessment)`, `make comments to the health practitioner`, `terminate the matter`, `refer the matter to the Director of Public Prosecutions`, `make a prohibition order or issue a public statement (s 41A)`
#ASSERT `What can the Commission do at the end of the investigation` `organisation` EQUALS LIST `terminate the matter`, `make recommendations or comments to the health organisation, with a report to the Health Secretary`, `refer the matter to the Director of Public Prosecutions`, `make a prohibition order or issue a public statement, if it is a relevant health organisation (s 45C)`

#ASSERT `Must I be told the results of the investigation` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Must I be told the results of the investigation` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

#ASSERT `Must the Commission review its decision after the investigation` TRUE `practitioner` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Must the Commission review its decision after the investigation` FALSE `practitioner` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Must the Commission review its decision after the investigation` TRUE `organisation` EQUALS NOTHING

#ASSERT `Can I have the report on the health organisation` TRUE `organisation` TRUE EQUALS `the Commission may give you a copy, at its discretion`
#ASSERT `Can I have the report on the health organisation` TRUE `organisation` FALSE EQUALS `there is no section 42(2) report, because the Commission made no recommendations or comments`
#ASSERT `Can I have the report on the health organisation` TRUE `practitioner` TRUE EQUALS `section 45(2A) does not provide for giving you a copy`
#ASSERT `Can I have the report on the health organisation` FALSE `organisation` TRUE EQUALS `section 45(2A) does not provide for giving you a copy`

-- ss 41B(3)(a), 45D(3)(a). Arguments: I am the complainant; the decision.
#ASSERT `Must I be given a statement of the prohibition decision` TRUE `a finding that the practitioner or organisation breached a code of conduct (s 41A or 45C)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Must I be given a statement of the prohibition decision` TRUE `a prohibition order (s 41A or 45C)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Must I be given a statement of the prohibition decision` TRUE `issuing, revoking or revising a public statement (s 41A or 45C)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Must I be given a statement of the prohibition decision` TRUE `an interim prohibition order (s 41AA or 45B)` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Must I be given a statement of the prohibition decision` FALSE `a prohibition order (s 41A or 45C)` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Must I be given a statement of the prohibition decision` FALSE `an interim prohibition order (s 41AA or 45B)` EQUALS JUST FALSE

#ASSERT `May the Director of Proceedings tell me whether my complaint will be prosecuted` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `May the Director of Proceedings tell me whether my complaint will be prosecuted` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

